  "material_notes": {
    "wall_ceiling": "White plaster scan; restrained warm mineral tint and 0.10–0.25 mm bump distance.",
    "oak": "UV input in metres; 1.83 m scan repeat; grain and tangent normal rotate together to U. Quiet object-random variation and measured roughness. Reference-match revision: oak HSV saturation/value 0.90/1.12, oak_edge 0.92/1.04, preserving original honey chroma instead of the earlier gray-washed 0.65/1.28 floor tint.",
    "linen": "Rough blue linen scan recolored nondestructively to warm oatmeal; original albedo retained. Source repeat 0.271 m; sofa/sage repeat 0.46 m. Sofa/sage recolor input range 0.20–0.56 preserves highlight yarn variation (about 43% of source linear luminance samples exceeded previous 0.42 upper limit). Curtains retain previous finer weave and tint range.",
    "rug": "Hessian 380 scan, original repeat 0.274 m. Full-room reference-match repeat 1.35 m gives about 8 mm jute bundles (source yarn period approximately 6 pixels of 1024); previous 0.47 m repeat made the weave subpixel in the wide camera. Rug edge repeat 0.90 m. Color input range 0.14–0.43 increases measured weave contrast by about 33%; height Bump distance 0.0038 m, strength 0.5. All original maps retained.",
    "sheer": "Thin surface diffuse/translucent/transparent mixture; keeps shadow rays enabled and filters light.",
    "travertine": "AmbientCG Travertine009 original PBR maps, warm honed tint in shader. Source is procedural, disclosed explicitly.",
    "box_mapping": "Object metres, apply scale. BOX uses derivatives of original scanned height; archived tangent-space OpenGL normals are used by UV oak, not incorrectly applied to BOX coordinates.",
    "minor_materials": "Bronze, glazed ceramic, soil, leaf, books and emission are authored procedural shaders; no downloaded raster source.",
    "external_media": "No private tokens, paid assets, or remote runtime dependencies. Existing coastal_seaview.png not copied or altered by this module."
